<!--
  ============================================================================
  ZZZ_BiomeWildAnimalDuplicates_Generated.xml    GENERATED - do not hand-edit
  ============================================================================
  Regenerate with biome_wildanimals_inlist_dupes.py, flag `xml`, writing to THIS
  file's path (Patches/ZZZ_BiomeWildAnimalDuplicates_Generated.xml - the ZZZ_
  prefix is load-bearing, see below, and must be kept on every regeneration):
      python3 src/RimMandrake/Utils/biome_wildanimals_inlist_dupes.py
  (⛔ the flags are spelled with two hyphens, which XML forbids inside a comment,
   so they are named rather than written out here. See the script's docstring.)

  Companion to AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Generated.xml (cross-registration: biome
  wildAnimals x animal race.wildBiomes) and AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Fix.xml's Blocks
  1-3 (same class, hand-verified). This file is the THIRD, DIFFERENT class: one
  BiomeDef's own <wildAnimals> list holding the SAME PawnKindDef twice - RimWorld's
  own BiomeDef.ConfigErrors() calls this out directly ("Duplicate animal record: X"),
  and it hits BiomeDef.CommonalityOfAnimal()'s Dictionary.Add() throw in the FIRST
  loop, before the cross-registration check even runs.

  🔴 THIS FILE'S NAME IS LOAD-BEARING, not cosmetic. RimWorld enumerates a single
  mod's Patches/ folder in filesystem order (DirectXmlLoader.XmlAssetsInModFolder,
  confirmed via RimSage against ModContentPack.LoadPatches / DirectoryInfo.GetFiles)
  and applies that mod's patches strictly in that order - no independent sort pass.
  The removal for a given pair must run after EVERY file in this mod that could add
  that pair a second time - which is not always the same file. First measured:
  AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Fix.xml's Block 4 sorted BEFORE BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml (A < B)
  and silently no-opped on all 7 live pairs it targeted (confirmed 2026-09-12 against
  capture 2026-09-12T19-16-27Z). Renamed once to "BiomeWildAnimalDuplicates_
  Generated.xml" (sorts after BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml) to fix that - but the VERY NEXT
  restart still showed AA_Eyeling duplicated on Wasteland/ExtremeDesert/
  ZBiome_DesertOasis, because `Ikee_Rename.xml` ALSO adds AA_Eyeling to those same
  three biomes (renaming it to "ikee" requires re-registering it in each biome's
  wildAnimals list under the new label) and "Ikee_Rename.xml" (I) sorts AFTER
  "BiomeWildAnimalDuplicates_Generated.xml" (B) - the removal ran, found only the ONE
  occurrence BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml had added so far, no-opped on the missing second
  index, and Ikee_Rename.xml then created the second occurrence anyway, untouched.
  ⇒ Renamed AGAIN to "ZZZ_BiomeWildAnimalDuplicates_Generated.xml" (Z sorts after
  every other current filename in this mod's Patches/ folder) so this sorts after
  everything in the folder by construction, not "after the one or two files I have
  in mind." Confirmed fixed 2026-09-12 against capture 2026-09-12T20-48-00Z. Do not rename this
  file to anything that would not still sort last among this folder's filenames -
  re-check the actual folder listing before ever renaming it again, this has already
  broken twice from checking too narrow a set of "the one file that adds this."

  Each removal targets the SECOND (or later) occurrence by XPath index, e.g.
  wildAnimals/Foo[2] - the biome's own commonality (our cast) is always kept, the
  donor's duplicate record is what goes. Multiple duplicates of the same pair remove
  from the HIGHEST index down, so an earlier removal never shifts a later target's
  index out from under it.

  Every op is a PatchOperationConditional: an absent mod, or a def that no longer
  collides, turns it into a silent no-op instead of a red error.
  Generated from capture 2026-09-12T20-48-00Z
  3 pair(s) found this run; 4 triple(s) carried from the previous file
  that this capture can no longer see (our own removals hide their own
  evidence once they take effect). 7 operation(s), the UNION of every
  triple ever found.
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- 1. AA_Eyeling x ExtremeDesert (record 2 of 2) -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ExtremeDesert"]/wildAnimals/AA_Eyeling[2]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ExtremeDesert"]/wildAnimals/AA_Eyeling[2]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- 2. AA_Eyeling x Wasteland (record 2 of 2) -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="Wasteland"]/wildAnimals/AA_Eyeling[2]</xpath>
